{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Behold, to YHWH your Elohim</b> — the verse begins and ends with heh, to teach that with heh the world was created, corresponding to the five books of the Torah. And ten words are in the verse, to teach that the Shekhinah did not descend below ten." "<b>the earth and all that is in it</b> — and adjacent to it is רק באבותיך. To teach that the earth and all that is in it was created only in the merit of the patriarchs. רק באבותיך is a limitation — that even upon them there is judgment. Abraham: במה אדע. Isaac loved Esau. Jacob said: נסתרה דרכי מה׳. It is juxtaposed: רק באבותיך and מלתם, to teach that you shall circumcise the foreskin of the heart just as the patriarchs did."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:21.577192137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}